# Lesson 4, part 3: holding period return (HPR). Source: the lesson 3 base file, the HPR definition and the Burkits, Mavericks and Lipaz questions,
# and question 4 of its homework (Yuval). The house definition: what the holder received over the holding period, coupons and the sale price, over the price paid, minus 1.
assert round(_fin.RATE(5, 56, -744, 800), 4) == 0.0879
assert round(((112 + 760) / 744) ** .5 - 1, 4) == 0.0826
_pm = -_fin.PV(0.03, 8, 28, 800)
assert round(_pm, 2) == 828.08 and round(((112 + _pm) / 811) ** .5 - 1, 4) == 0.0766
_pl = -_fin.PV(1.08243216 ** .25 - 1, 9, 12.5, 500)
assert round(_pl, 2) == 520.41 and round(((37.5 + _pl) / 495) ** (4 / 3) - 1, 4) == 0.1729

